RF.put("questb:b75",{"8795":{"id":8795,"t":"The Alliance Needs Your Help!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 49.","obj":"Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.","desc":"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, ‹name›!\nYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, ‹class›? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","rew":"Experience: 650","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":32.9,"n":"Master Sergeant Fizzlebolt","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8155":{"id":8155,"t":"Arathi Basin Resources!","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!\nThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.\nThat is what I want from you, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Do you have the resource crate, ‹name›? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...","done":"You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.\nThank you, ‹name›. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\nLevel 25 , requires level 20 Difficulty 20 21 23 28 33 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8155","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8395":{"id":8395,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"635":{"id":635,"t":"Crystal in the Mountains","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the crystal from your vision.\nProvided: Pendant of Myzrael","desc":"This shard pulses as you hold it...\nYou feel a sense of pleading coming from the shard, as if someone is trying to communicate, someone who desperately needs your help.\nA vision appears in your mind - of the northern mountains of Arathi, and of a brilliant crystal jutting from the earth there.\nYou feel drawn to that place.","rew":"Experience: 280","done":"This crystal pulses, as if a living force is trapped within it.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":62.5,"y":33.7,"n":"Shards of Myzrael","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1035":{"id":1035,"t":"Fallen Sky Lake","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve a Fallen Moonstone from the Shadethicket Oracle, then bring it to Pelturas in Astranaar.\nFallen Moonstone Shadethicket Oracle","desc":"Relara's fever has passed, but she is still very weak. I do not believe time alone will give her back the strength she has lost. I believe it will take the power of a moonstone.\nWe used to gather moonstones at Fallen Sky Lake to the southeast... until the Shadethickets came.\nTheir leader, a Shadethicket Oracle, gathered up all the fallen moonstones and hoards them. Now, you must retrieve a moonstone from the Oracle.\nAnd to do that, I fear that you must slay him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSnapbrook Armor Beastial Manacles Luminescent Amice\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Did you face the Shadethicket Oracle, ‹name›? If so, then please hand me the fallen moonstone. Relara has strength left for only a few more breaths!","done":"Oh, ‹name›, you have saved my daughter! I know the power of the moonstone will give back my daughter her strength!\nI can never repay you fully for the aid you have given me, but... please, take this. Other than Relara, it is my most dear possession.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":37.4,"y":51.8,"n":"Pelturas Whitemoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"715":{"id":715,"t":"Liquid Stone","lv":37,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Healing Potion and a Lesser Invisibility Potion to Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands.\nHealing Potion Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver 50 % , Qiraji Lieutenant Jo-rel 45 % , Minor Anubisath Warbringer 40 % , Qiraji Lieutenant 40 % and 4 more\nLesser Invisibility Potion","desc":"I'm thinking those items you acquired for Lotwil are going to be the least of our worries, ‹name›. On the other hand, you've proven more than adept at the sciences Lotwil holds sacred, so how about helping me out?\nI need an invisibility potion and a healing potion; both might come in handy real soon if he pulls this off.\nIn return, I'll give you this recipe for a potion I've been developing while learning from Lotwil. It's based on some of the research he's been doing here in the Badlands.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Lesser Stoneshield Potion 2 Lesser Stoneshield Potion\nExperience: 2,100","back":"He's getting closer to finishing. How are things going on your end?","done":"YES!\nI mean, thank you, ‹name›. These will be helpful while traveling through the Badlands.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Lucien Tosselwrench","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"795":{"id":795,"t":"Seal of the Earth","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 50 instead of 55.","obj":"Diamond Runestone Scalding Whelp , Pillar of Diamond\nOpal Runestone Scalding Whelp , Pillar of Opal\nAmethyst Runestone Scalding Whelp , Scorched Guardian , Pillar of Amethyst","back":"The Seal of the Earth lies here, with three recessed alcoves for the Amethyst Runestone, the Opal Runestone, and the Diamond Runestone.","done":"As you place the Runestones into the matching recesses, a violent rumbling shakes the earth as the Seal is broken.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":81.5,"y":49.9,"n":"Seal of the Earth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"1275":{"id":1275,"t":"Researching the Corruption","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Staghide Armguards. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine wants 8 Corrupt Brain stems.\n8 Corrupted Brain Stem Blackfathom Myrmidon 80 % , Blackfathom Sea Witch 80 % , Blackfathom Oracle 80 % , Blackfathom Tide Priestess 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Foolish blood elves toil with demonic magic. Have they not witnessed what happened with the naga and with the satyrs of Kalimdor?\nI fear that the blood elves will meet a similar deformation. Azeroth cannot afford to give birth to another vile race of monsters.\nI wish to study the brain stems of the satyr and naga so that I might deduce what fate the elves are headed toward. In Blackfathom Deeps, on the coast of Ashenvale, you will find both satyr and naga.\n'Tis a long journey, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBeetle Clasps Prelacy Cape Staghide Armguards\nNew in Forever: Staghide Armguards.\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,400\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Once I have enough samples to study, my true work can begin. With the corrupted brain stems of both the satyr and naga of Blackfathom Deeps I can try to draw a correlation between the mutations.\nPerhaps with that gained knowledge we can prevent the blood elves from delving deeper into deformity and evil.","done":"You have traveled far and undoubtedly faced great peril.\nYour actions have been selfless. 'Tis for the good of all Azeroth that you help me with my research. I thank you, ‹name›, for all that you have done.\nNow if you'll excuse me I have much work to do....","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.3,"y":43,"n":"Gershala Nightwhisper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"97915":{"id":97915,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Alchemist Mallory in Elwynn Forest near Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":39.8,"y":48.4,"n":"Alchemist Mallory","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94315":{"id":94315,"t":"Craftsmans writ earthen silk belt","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Earthen Silk Belt\nEarthen Silk Belt","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Earthen Silk Belt, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Earthen Silk Belt Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94315","cats":["crafting"]},"94235":{"id":94235,"t":"Craftsmans writ gnomish universal remote","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Gnomish Universal Remote\nGnomish Universal Remote","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Gnomish Universal Remote, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Careful where you walk, Gizmo! This thing likes to activate when you least expect it, and we don't quite have a handle on where it can take you when we aren't actively manning the controls.","done":"Seems we are in luck, the remote has arrived! Looks like you precalibrated it for us which, I'll admit, isn't ideal for this scenario.\nI should be able to reverse engineer it in no time. Then maybe, hopefully, I'll be able to take a much needed break. Feels like I've been stuck fumbling with this teleporter's controls for months on end!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.6,"y":77.4,"n":"Scooty","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"955":{"id":955,"t":"Bashal'Aran","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 8 Grell Earrings for Asterion in Bashal'Aran.\n8 Grell Earring Wild Grell 48 % , Vile Sprite 48 %","desc":"If I were to relate the story of my life, I have no doubt it would surpass the limits of your patience. Let us say that mine has been a long and painful life, and this spectral form is perhaps the worst torment of all.\nI am held here by the means of magic. Though my words may seem disingenuous, I assure you I would be grateful beyond words if you would help me find the means of my imprisonment. A seal binds me, and by examining the earpieces of the sprites and grells, I may find a trace of it.","rew":"Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Once I have the earrings, I will cast the spell to search for the whereabouts of the seal that binds me. For centuries I have thought on the freedom destroying the seal would bring to me... Perhaps those centuries have taken a toll upon my mind that I might never recover...","done":"Indeed... The grells of Bashal'Aran do not possess that which I am searching... however they have come into contact with it recently. Recently... I would reckon that by your time, not mine. Recent for me stretches into the veil of the past, almost another Age...","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":44.2,"y":36.3,"n":"Asterion","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"7675":{"id":7675,"t":"Icy Blue Mechanostrider Replacement","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Icy Blue Mechanostrider Mod A","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Green Mechanostrider Swift White Mechanostrider Swift Yellow Mechanostrider","back":"[PH] If you bring me your old fast mechanostrider, I will trade it in for one from the new pack. The new mechanostrider will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift mechanostriders we already have around the yard here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.1,"y":48,"n":"Milli Featherwhistle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"315":{"id":315,"t":"The Perfect Stout","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Shimmerweeds to Rejold Barleybrew in the Brewnall Village.\n6 Shimmerweed Shimmerweed Basket , Frostmane Seer 75 %","desc":"I'm on a quest, a quest to make the perfect stout. I know I can do it -- brewing's in my blood. I just need to find the right recipe...\nThe Frostmane trolls grow a plant, shimmerweed, high up in the hills to the east. They use it in their strange, tribal rituals. We dwarves haven't found much use for it, but it has a unique taste...and I want to experiment with it in my brews!\nGet me some shimmerweed from Frostmane seers, or swipe it from the trolls' shimmerweed baskets.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGoat Fur Cloak Ivy-weave Bracers\nExperience: 775\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Do you have that Shimmerweed? I almost have a batch of stout ready to brew, and I want to try throwing the weed in with this mixture.","done":"Great! I can't wait to use these in some of my recipes. There's one in particular I think it'll work great in...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.7,"n":"Rejold Barleybrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96875":{"id":96875,"t":"Beasts of thunder ridge","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kamari in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Rough Lizard Hide from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 2 Cured Light Hides.\n5 Rough Lizard Hide\n2 Cured Light Hide","desc":"Orgrimmar is always expanding, ‹class›. And when the peons need hides to line the walls and roofs of our new buildings, they come to me!\nThe hides of the lizards in Thunder Ridge are typically too thick for armor, but they make excellent building material. Bring me some of their hides, along with a few lighter cured hides. Let's see your skill with leather!","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Light Leather Reagent Bag\nMoney: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yes?","done":"Your work helps Orgrimmar grow. Know that as you walk the city's paths.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63,"y":45,"n":"Kamari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"75":{"id":75,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Marshal Haggard wants you to check the chest upstairs for the Faded Journal Page.\nA Faded Journal Page Marshal Haggard's Chest","desc":"There was a bundle of parchments in the chest upstairs when I moved into this place. I looked at them once when I first arrived but I gave up once the fog hazed over my peepers.\nDo an old, nearly-blind man a favor and check the chest upstairs for anything that might help you in your quest to discover more about this Stalvan character. I'm pretty sure there's a faded journal page that might be of interest to you. Bring it to me and I'll help in anyway I can.","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find that page I mentioned, ‹name›?","done":"You found it!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.6,"y":69.4,"n":"Marshal Haggard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9195":{"id":9195,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Goblin Sapper Charge","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 20 Goblin Sapper Charges and the Craftsman's Writ - Goblin Sapper Charge - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Goblin Sapper Charge\n20 Goblin Sapper Charge\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Goblin Sapper Charge","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order EN-11:\n20 Goblin Sapper Charges.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"Now you're talking my language, ‹class›. Things that go BOOM!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"555":{"id":555,"t":"Soothing Turtle Bisque","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 pieces of Turtle Meat and some Soothing Spices to Chef Jessen in Southshore.\n10 Turtle Meat Giant Surf Glider 53 % , Coralshell Tortoise 46.7 % , Saltwater Snapjaw 40.8 % , Mudrock Tortoise 40.6 % and 4 more\nSoothing Spices sold by Gunder Thornbush , sold by Banalash , sold by Nerrist , sold by Edna Mullby and 4 more","desc":"If there's one thing you'll learn about Southshore it's that we have some of the best cuisine north of Stormwind!\nTake my secret recipe for Turtle Bisque, for example. I've known folks to travel from as far as Darkshire just to enjoy a bowl. Speaking of which, I haven't been able to make any lately. I used to head up past Dalaran to Lake Lordamere myself to hunt Snapjaws but it's just too dangerous now. If you bring me some Turtle Meat from the Snapjaws up north and Soothing Spices, I'll whip some up!","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Soothing Turtle Bisque 3 Soothing Turtle Bisque\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Any luck finding the ingredients? I'll tell you, this territory isn't the peaceful place it once was. Ah, if only this unrest never occurred...","done":"Everyone will be so pleased: Chef Jessen's Soothing Turtle Bisque is served once again!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.9,"y":58.7,"n":"Chef Jessen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6075":{"id":6075,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Grif Wildheart in Kharanos. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, I do believe you are ready, as well....","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":34.4,"n":"Regnus Thundergranite","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8955":{"id":8955,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Devout Sandals, Devout Skirt and Devout Mantle.\nDevout Sandals Maleki the Pallid 0 % in Stratholme\nDevout Skirt Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nDevout Mantle Solakar Flamewreath 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Sandals Virtuous Skirt Virtuous Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8715":{"id":8715,"t":"Bladeleaf the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.3,"y":60.8,"n":"Elder Bladeleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8635":{"id":8635,"t":"Splitrock the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The battles of ages past are seeds from which legends grow. Yours is a time of heroes, young one. May your legend take root, thrive.\nI bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...\nStart Elder Splitrock End Elder Splitrock Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 8635","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8875":{"id":8875,"t":"The Lunar Festival","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger at the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.","desc":"It's that time of the year, ‹name›! The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival. You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight. She can tell you more about the holiday.","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Are you here to join in the festivities?\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":40.8,"y":30.5,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":38.4,"y":63.4,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.8,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9115":{"id":9115,"t":"Sandals of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Sandals of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Sandals, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Sandals Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nSandals of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you brought me the reagents, child?","done":"The vestments are ready, ‹name›. Smite those that would harm our world in your righteous fire.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"97275":{"id":97275,"t":"Whuuts the rush","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Give Yelmak's Potion to Whuut.\nProvided: Yelmak's Potion","desc":"Whuut is a prodigy. That much is true. But he doesn't yet have the experience, wisdom, and time on the stirring rod to know how to respect alchemical processes.\nHe is exhausting all of the rarest and most exotic reagents we have available without pausing to practice and refine his basic skills.\nGive him this potion I've brewed with a quick tonic method. He'll reconsider everything he's doing when he learns how local remedies and careful touch are the first true mastery.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n2 Lesser Mana Potion 2 Healing Potion\nExperience: 800","back":"Alright, what's next... Black Lotus, Mountain Silversage...","done":"Grorru--whaa?\nYou say Yelmak made this potion from speargrass and cattail with no other reagents? I didn't know chemists had any real need for these common plants we see every day.\nMaybe he's right. There could be a lot I'm missing out on by skipping to the most rare and least-studied flora first.\nDrakath, take your pick from one of these potions I brewed earlier. I appreciate you taking the time to visit our shop.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.6,"y":33.2,"n":"Yelmak","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.8,"y":33.2,"n":"Whuut","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"235":{"id":235,"t":"The Ashenvale Hunt","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.","desc":"Attention, young adventurers! The wilds of Ashenvale await you!\nThe Horde has established a strong presence in the lands north of the Barrens. Our two outposts - Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand Outpost - strive to bring glory to the Horde! Those who would prove themselves should seek out guidance there. Of note: Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post, directly north of the Barrens, seeks adventurers willing to take part in a great hunt of Ashenvale!","rew":"Experience: 160\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Welcome to the new frontier, ‹name›. Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young ‹class› like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle. Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.\nYour presence here tells me that you've come to learn more about the hunt. Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.\nOrgrimmar Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":66.1,"n":"Warcaller Gorlach","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1435":{"id":1435,"t":"The Burning of Spirits","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Burning Gem and 15 Infused Burning Gems to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\nBurning Gem\n15 Infused Burning Gem\nProvided: Burning Gem","desc":"Death is most desirable for those despicable creatures that turn their back on their liege for such selfish reasons. But death is not enough when dealing with those that have given themselves over to the darkness.\nTake this gem. When one of the Burning Blade's near death, activate its magic. The spell shall pull the corrupted spirit out of its victim, leaving an infused gem behind.\nBring me these infused gems so I may dispose of them properly.\nGo now, and may you elude death.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I have tried to make the magics as simple as possible. Drawing the spirit of your victim out of its injured form should be child's play. Do not rely on the gem's power to slay your foe completely. You must only activate the gem when they are close to death, or it will be useless.","done":"Ah, you've returned successful. That is good. Give me the gems and I shall put them someplace safe....\nMy tasks for you are complete, ‹class›. Speak to Takata when you are rested. He may have other tasks for you, or perhaps needs you to return to Orgrimmar to inform Keldran of our progress here in Desolace.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.2,"y":53.4,"n":"Maurin Bonesplitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7835":{"id":7835,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by the Darkspear Trolls, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37.7,"y":87.9,"n":"Vehena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5675":{"id":5675,"t":"Elune's Grace","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"Time's a wastin', lad/lass. It's time for you to return home to Darnassus. Priestess Alathea's sent word here that you're to return there for training. Seems they feel you're ready to be tested much like those who serve the Light. You should head out whenever you can. Alathea's message said that she'd be waitin' for you in the Temple of the Moon. Good luck.","rew":"You will learn: Elune's Grace\nExperience: 390","done":"Elune bless you for returning so quickly to us. This is an important time in your training, and a time that all of our order take very seriously. When you've rested from your journey here, please, let me know. We can then discuss the continuation of your training and where your path will lead you next.\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8235":{"id":8235,"t":"Encoded Fragments","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Encoded Fragments to Archmage Xylem in Azshara.\n10 Encoded Fragment Forest Ooze 80 % , Thunderhead Stagwing 80 % , Thunderhead Skystormer 80 % , Thunderhead Patriarch 80 % and 2 more","desc":"Lord Ravenholdt has asked a favor of us both. He wishes to remove the enchantment from this bag.\nUnfortunately, some of my books on the subject of dispelling were taken recently, only to be destroyed by savages. The remains of my books are still valuable to me.\nIf you can bring me enough of the encoded fragments, I can piece them back together. Your best chance is to kill the beasts of Azshara, since they have a tendency to pick up just about anything.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Ravenholdt","back":"Have you found enough fragments to continue my work?","done":"It looks like you picked up some of the better fragments. Perhaps you aren't worthless after all.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"95195":{"id":95195,"t":"Bloodied Insignia","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Collect 10 Bloodied Insignias and take them to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind City.\nProvided: 10 Bloodied Insignia","desc":"<The old Alliance insignia appears to have belonged to a soldier of Lordaeron. These ruins are likely filled with similar medals that living relatives would be grateful to have returned to them.>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDuty Bound Leggings Remembrance Armor\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"You look as if you're carrying a heavy burden, Black. What is it?","done":"Your instincts to bring these to me were not unfounded. When Lordaeron fell to the scourge, many people fled to take refuge here in Stormwind. There are likely few who remain to claim these insignias themselves.\nYour duty to Stormwind is commended, Black. I'll begin distributing these tokens to next of kin right away.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.8,"y":75.4,"n":"General Marcus Jonathan","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"5515":{"id":5515,"t":"Krastinov's Bag of Horrors","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate Jandice Barov in the Scholomance and destroy her. From her corpse recover Krastinov's Bag of Horrors. Return the bag to Eva Sarkhoff.\nKrastinov's Bag of Horrors Jandice Barov in Scholomance","desc":"A great weight has been lifted from our hearts, ‹name›, but your task is not yet complete. Krastinov's master, Kirtonos, still lives.\nBefore you may face Kirtonos, however, you must first secure a method in which to summon him.\nIt is said that Jandice Barov stewards the blood of innocents from Krastinov to Kirtonos.\nFind her in the sunken catacombs of Scholomance and strike her down. Bring back any clues that you may find.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"<Eva fades in and out of focus.>","done":"The bag of horrors!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.2,"y":73.7,"n":"Eva Sarkhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"93035":{"id":93035,"t":"Ravaging ravagers","lv":38,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan and slay 6 Undead Ravagers, then return to Nerlokh at the southern entrance to Valley of Bones.\nUndead Ravager x 6\nGelkis Clan Centaur:\nLevel 38 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 41 48 Side Both factions Quest ID 93035\nThe chain\n10 quests from level 32 to 38, 14,740 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Strange Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Raid on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Gelkis Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 35 ] Stealing Supplies\nBring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n1,350 XP\n4 [ 37 ] Ongeku\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,850 XP\n5 [ 38 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Gelkis, and locate Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones far east of Gelkis Village.\n290 XP\n6 [ 38 ] Ravaging Ravagers this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan and slay 6 Undead Ravagers, then return to Nerlokh at the southern entrance to Valley of Bones.\n1,450 XP\n7 [ 38 ] Facing the Truth\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n700 XP\n8 [ 38 ] A Cleansing Cry\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n2,150 XP\n9 [ 38 ] Test Your Theory\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and dispel the necromantic curse present on the Accursed Skull.\n700 XP","cats":["shendralas"]},"8315":{"id":8315,"t":"The Calling","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to recover the Crystal Unlocking Mechanism from the Qiraji Emissary.\nYou have been instructed to take the Glyphs of Calling to the Bones of Grakkarond, south of Cenarion Hold, and draw them in the sand. Should the Qiraji Emissary appear, slay it and recover the Crystal Unlocking Mechanism. Return to Geologist Larksbane if you succeed.\nAssemble an army for this task, ‹name›!\nCrystal Unlocking Mechanism Emissary Roman'khan\nProvided: Glyphs of Calling","desc":"The glyphs illustrate an emissary of the Qiraji meeting with three silithid at the bones of a large dragon. Above the glyphs is what I can only assume to be a code of some sort. This code might very well be the key to summoning the emissary.\nI will create a copy of the glyph code that you must use in the sand at the Bones of Grakkarond. If I am right, the Overlords will come thinking that new data is ready for transmission. Strike them down and confront the emissary. He holds the key to the crystals...","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You must take the opportunity as it presents itself and strike!","done":"I hold 20,000 years of history in my hands, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"84395":{"id":84395,"t":"Undead potatoes","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Undead Potatoes","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nUndead Potatoes (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"395":{"id":395,"t":"Brotherhood's End","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 625 experience instead of 325, 1.92 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Baros Alexston in Stormwind.","desc":"Ah, I almost forgot. Alexston came while you were away, he wished to speak with you. No doubt he wishes to report the goings-on of the Defias Brotherhood to the nobles.\nA bit of advice, ‹name›: if anyone should ask, I would provide all details but that it was your hand that slew Lescovar. Trust me. I am... acquainted... with the ways of such things.\nAnd as far as Trias goes, well, speak to no one of him... ever... if you can help it.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"It's good to see you, ‹name›. I have heard that Lord Gregor Lescovar was found dead not long ago.\nIt would seem that you were successful in your mission. You have my gratitude that you have saved me, and many others, from VanCleef's revenge.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8075":{"id":8075,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Augur's Hauberk","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Tabard. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Tabard\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The augurs of the Zandalar all wear a distinctive chest piece called a hauberk. It's fitted with the finest of silks and cloths, interwoven with strong chain. It's a symbol of not only their divinity, but also of their authority, mon. It's never wise to cross one whose life is devoted to speakin' with the spirits...\nBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us. Do it and I'll give ya one of the finest hauberks our augurs would ever hope to wear!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Augur's Hauberk\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"The Paragons of Power are a key source of magic power - the same kind of power that goes into makin' the augur's hauberk. Bring me what I need, and I'll be able to share the finest of vestments any Zandalar augur would be wantin' as their own.","done":"I know what ya had to go through to bring me the Paragons of Power, ‹name›. It wasn't easy, mon - defeatin' the evil that seeps out of Zul'Gurub like a foul ooze - but now that it is all said and done, I can easily say that you'll be revered amongst the Zandalar for ages to come!\nHere - take the augur's hauberk and wear it with pride!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"2875":{"id":2875,"t":"WANTED: Andre Firebeard","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Andre's Head to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle in Steamwheedle Port.\nFirebeard's Head Andre Firebeard","desc":"The vile pirate Andre Firebeard is wanted for crimes against Steamwheedle and Gadgetzan.\nBy decree of governing counsel, any who read this are hereby authorized to use lethal force during the apprehension of Andre and his abettors.\nBy further decree, should Andre be deceased, or otherwise indisposed, during the time of his hearing, his head may act as proxy, and deliverance of such head to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle constitutes a binding, and tenderable, contract.","rew":"Money: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"You look a little dazed. Have you been reading our legal documents?","done":"Ah, Andre's head. So I guess he'll make his trial after all!\nMuch appreciated, ‹name›. Now if you'll just sign here, I can issue you payment for services rendered.\nDon't worry about the small print. It's harmless, and... I don't think there's a magnifying glass small enough to read it anyway.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.8,"y":22.3,"n":"Wanted Poster","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.8,"y":27,"n":"Wanted Poster","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":67.1,"y":23.9,"n":"Security Chief Bilgewhizzle","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8555":{"id":8555,"t":"The Charge of the Dragonflights","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"Eranikus, Vaelastrasz, and Azuregos... No doubt you know of these dragons, mortal. It is no coincidence, then, that they have played such influential roles as watchers of our world.\nUnfortunately (and my own naivety is partially to blame) whether by agents of the Old Gods or betrayal by those that would call them friend, each guardian has fallen to tragedy. The extent of which has fueled my own distrust towards your kind.\nSeek them out... And ‹race›, prepare yourself for the worst.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"475":{"id":475,"t":"A Troubling Breeze","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Gaerolas Talvethren in Starbreeze Village.","desc":"A troubling breeze blows through the forest.\nGaerolas Talvethren serves as Great Warden to the hibernating Druids of the Talon in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. His duty as the chosen protector of the Sleeping is to ensure their safety so that their pact with Ysera remains fulfilled.\nBut word from Gaerolas is now delayed and I grow nervous. Travel east to Starbreeze Village and bring back a report from Gaerolas so that I can put my worries to rest, knowing my dreaming brethren slumber safely.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Thank the forest spirits you are here! I knew Athridas would sense trouble and send help.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56,"y":57.3,"n":"Athridas Bearmantle","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":66.3,"y":58.5,"n":"Gaerolas Talvethren","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"875":{"id":875,"t":"Harpy Lieutenants","lv":16,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Harpy Lieutenant Rings from Witchwing Slayers and return them to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.\n6 Harpy Lieutenant Ring Witchwing Slayer 80 %","desc":"Hahaha, ‹name›. Back for more? Good, I like to hear that.\nThis time I want you to assassinate some of the harpy lieutenants in the Dry Hills. Only Witchwing Slayers can be lieutenants, and you can tell them apart by the rings they carry. They are a nasty bunch, but they lead some of the underlings in that area. Taking out 6 of them will be a decisive strike against their matriarchy.\nMake sure they die painfully, ‹name›. We want those harpy wenches to know the idiocy of picking fights with the Horde.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have 6 Harpy Lieutenant Rings yet? Justice must be dealt to them for their vicious attacks on the Horde.","done":"Excellent work my friend. I think you'll go far within the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.6,"y":30.9,"n":"Darsok Swiftdagger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96395":{"id":96395,"t":"An Ancient Grudge","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Put the spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar to rest and then return to the Ghostly Attendant in the Hall of Thanes.\nFaldrim Anvilmar slain","desc":"The... Thane... my mighty... Thane... he... needs to... rest.\nPlease... help him... help him... rest...\nConsumed... by... ancient... grudge... No... rest...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCatacomb Cloak Deepgrave Trousers\nExperience: 2,300\nStart Ghostly Attendant The Hall of Thanes Level 15 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 11 13 18 22 Side Both factions Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 96395","cats":["the-hall-of-thanes"]},"98155":{"id":98155,"t":"Pristine pesterhide pelts","lv":31,"min":27,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 5 Pristine Pesterhide Pelts to Kristy Grant.\n5 Pristine Pesterhide Pelt","desc":"The Pesterhide hyenas of Thousand Needles have the most gorgeous coats. I haven't seen such a brilliant hue of fur like that in all of my travels!\nI would like to send back some pelts to my sisters back in Stormwind, as I know they could make something incredible out of them.\nI don't have any fighting experience, so I would be very grateful if you could gather some of the Pesterhide pelts in my stead.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\nFeralas Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":89.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Kristy Grant","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1115":{"id":1115,"t":"The Rumormonger","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Krazek in Booty Bay.","desc":"Now that we've done a service for the gnomes, it's time to do the goblins a favor!\nI hear that the goblin racer pilot, Nazz Steamboil, didn't always use that name. I wonder why he changed it. I wonder if it's a secret, and... I wonder if he values that secret.\nIf anyone knows the truth, then it's Krazek of Booty Bay, on the southern tip of Stranglethorn. Speak with Krazek and ask him about our goblin pilot.\nIf you can get useful information from him, then we might just turn a profit from it.","rew":"Experience: 1,400","done":"You want to know about Nazz Steamboil? He's a racer pilot out in the Shimmering Flats, isn't he?\nYeah, I might be able to find something out about him... but it won't be easy. Or fast.\nOr cheap.\nThousand Needles Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1195":{"id":1195,"t":"The Sacred Flame","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return a Filled Etched Phial to Zangen Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\nFilled Etched Phial","desc":"The Galak centaur in the Thousand Needles are protecting an artifact from the time of the centaurs' creation.\nWe would like to retrieve it, but we require a phial of water from one of the night elves' moonwells.\nTo collect the water, you will first need to obtain one of the phials carried by the dryads near the Raynewood Retreat in the heart of Ashenvale Forest. There is a moonwell near the western bank of the Falfarren River, south of the main road, where you can fill the phial.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Once we have the filled phial, we can send it along to my associate, Rau, in the Thousand Needles. He was the one who requested the phial of water, so he'll better know how we can make use of it.","done":"Very good. This should fill Rau's request just fine. Could you deliver this to him? You might enjoy spending some time out in the Needles.\nThunder Bluff Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":55,"y":51.4,"n":"Zangen Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"6395":{"id":6395,"t":"Marla's Last Wish","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.","obj":"Bring Samuel Fipps' Remains to Marla's Grave, then return to Novice Elreth.\nSamuel's Remains Buried","desc":"My friend Marla Fipps lived with her husband Samuel before the plague, but when the plague came Samuel succumbed and joined the Scourge's ranks.\nMarla was spared an undeath only to die at the hands of her now mindless husband. So strong was her love, however, that her last dying wish was to be buried with her beloved Samuel.\nSamuel Fipps roams at a ruined camp along the road northeast of Deathknell. Defeat him and grant Marla's wish: bury him at her grave, in the first row of our graveyard.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nNew in Forever: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.\nExperience: 450\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"We must respect our dead, ‹name›. It is one of the ways in which we differ from the Scourge...","done":"You have done a good deed today, ‹name›. Although our struggle against the Scourge continues, let us hope that Marla and Samuel will find peace together in their final resting place.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.9,"y":66.1,"n":"Novice Elreth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"3115":{"id":3115,"t":"Tainted Memorandum","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Tainted Memorandum and speak to Alamar Grimm inside Anvilmar above Coldridge Valley.\nTainted Memorandum\nProvided: Tainted Memorandum","desc":"While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the warlock trainer Alamar. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.\nAnd watch yerself, ‹name›, your kind ain't too trusted 'round these parts.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Wonderful! You got my memorandum obviously.\nIgnore the fools around you, ‹name›. The Holy Light?! The sword and shield?! These aren't paths for ones as open minded as us. Look at what \"normal\" magic did to our home. Coupled with those damned tinkerers, our race almost became extinct. And now we have to rely on the dwarves-- they'd rather spend time allying with humans than help us rebuild our own home. We're like second-class citizens. Have you seen the way they look at us?","done":"But none of that matters. What matters is that you've seen your own Holy Light! You know where power truly comes from. You realize that having our own allies is much more... prudent. Special allies. Allies that, no matter the task, will obey till their last breath.\nAnd that's where I come in, ‹name›. I can train you in the beginnings of those special powers. Seek me out often and I will do what I can to teach you more spells.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.6,"y":66.1,"n":"Alamar Grimm","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1515":{"id":1515,"t":"Dogran's Captivity","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ken'zigla's Draught to Dogran in the Barrens.\nKen'zigla's Draught\nProvided: Ken'zigla's Draught","desc":"You've made it this far, so if you want to see this through to the end, I won't stop you. I can't spare you any additional manpower though, you'll be on your own.\nDogran is being held in a quilboar camp to the north of here. Look for a group of two huts. He'll be heavily guarded--that is, if they haven't killed him yet, or he hasn't succumbed to his wounds.\nGood luck.","rew":"Experience: 1,150","back":"Urrrghhhh...","done":"Foul tasting brew...\nI can feel the strength in me now, enough to hobble away... But my leg, I will have lost it for the rest of my life. My arm, too.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.6,"y":59.3,"n":"Grunt Logmar","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.3,"y":47.9,"n":"Grunt Dogran","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"155":{"id":155,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,700 experience instead of 1,650, 1.03 times as much.","obj":"Escort the Defias Traitor to the secret hideout of the Defias Brotherhood. Once the Defias Traitor shows you where VanCleef and his men are hiding out, return to Gryan Stoutmantle with the information.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"So Stoutmantle sends a scrawny ‹race› like you to protect me? Guess you'll have to do. Better bring some friends too.\nYou know the deal, right? You watch my back and I'll take you to the Defias hideout. But you better be close by my side. The Defias gang wants my head now. If they see me with you, they'll try to kill me.\nLet me know when you and any friends you can round up are ready to go.","rew":"Experience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What business do you have with me? I am a very busy man...","done":"Most excellent, ‹name›! VanCleef is as good as ours now that we know where he is hiding.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":55.7,"y":47.5,"n":"The Defias Traitor","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"93835":{"id":93835,"t":"Confront lorthuna","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with High Priestess Lorthuna.\nConfront Lorthuna","desc":"Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Elaadrin and help them stop Lorthuna.\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBelt of Blades Empyrean Shoes Empyrean Greatsword Empyrean Treads\nMoney: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+150 reputation with Windshapers\n+150 reputation with High Order","done":"I sent a few of our remaining mages to ensure that Valennia and her forces were able to escape as well. She should be resting at High Elder Shadowsong's residence now.\nAnsirem had to return to Azeroth, but he and I discussed the next steps for the High Order before he departed. We survived the day, but Zephras is dangerously vulnerable now and we must make plans for what is to come.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":65.2,"y":50.4,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});